    "final_text": "I added a v2.4.0 section to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, written in the same style as the earlier entries. The version and date come from the `VERSION` and `RELEASE_DATE` files.\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * CSV export for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads on HTTP 503 with backoff (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when the config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in the monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\nI left out ACME-421 as you asked. It's the one marked as a breaking change (`!`, removing the `--legacy` flag from sync), so with it reverted this release has no breaking changes. That fits a minor version bump to 2.4.0. As with the older entries, I didn't include author names.",
